  "comments": [
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "value": "Cytotoxic protein, part of the enterotoxin complex. Responsible for binding to erythrocytes. This enterotoxin is thought to be the cause of the diarrheal form of gastroenteritis caused by food-borne strains of B.cereus"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "value": "Composed of a binding component, B, and two lytic components, L1 and L2. All three subunits act synergically to cause hemolysis"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "SUBUNIT"
    },
